  "paper": "brownian-motion",
  "argument": "arg-bm-diffusion-equation",
  "title": "The density one interval later",
  "spoken": "p of x and t plus tau equals the integral, over every jump Delta from minus infinity to infinity, of p of x minus Delta and t, times phi of Delta.",
  "explanation": "A particle found at x after one more interval tau was somewhere else a jump earlier. Add up every jump Delta that could have brought it: the density at x minus Delta now, times how likely a jump of that size is.",
